per is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-lcm-gap-engine"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-lcm-gap-engine"],"id":"long.thm-lcm-gap-engine","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.17 (Irrationality from a gap beyond the preceding least common multiple)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.17, p. 49, label thm:lcm-gap-engine","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For an integer base $b\\ge2$ and strictly increasing support $a:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb N$ with $a(0)\\ge\n1$: if $a(k)-\\mathrm{lcm}(a(0),\\dots,a(k-1))\\to\\infty$, then $\\sum'_k 1/(b^{a(k)}-1)$ is irrational. The base may vary over the integers, but the denominators remain $b^{a(k)}-1$. Applying the argument to another denominator sequence would require its own divisibility and tail estimates.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-lcm-gap-engine","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-lcm-gap-engine","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-lcm-gap-engine%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSum_of_lcm_gap%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-lcm-gap-engine%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSum_of_lcm_gap%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSum_of_lcm_gap"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/evidence/mapping.long.thm-lcm-gap-engine","id":"field:0f179017ad263e4c1206629d72adad57c4af74d1835abb5e3285235d3dd81ab0","kind":"subject_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f